course: dictionary
lesson: 2737
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Wash fruit and vegetables before eating, because they may have dirt or chemicals on them.» Here dirt means unclean stuff you can wash off, not soil.
explain: «Monkeys groom each other, picking out dirt, dead skin and bugs, which keeps fur clean.» Dirt here is unclean matter stuck in fur. Always ask: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «A graze scrapes off the top layer of skin, and dirt left in it can cause an infection.» Dirt here is something that can make a cut go bad, so it is important to keep grazes clean. When a word has several meanings, the sentence around it decides which one you need.
fact: Dirt means anything that makes things unclean, like mud, dust or grease.
fact: Dirt can also mean loose earth or soil, which is where plants grow and worms live.
fact: Dirt can mean gossip, or bad secret information about someone; this meaning is informal.
fact: Dirt can carry germs, so wash your hands after playing outside and before eating.
fact: «Dirt cheap» means very cheap, and a «dirt road» is a road with no hard surface.
exercise: «Wash fruit and vegetables before eating, because they may have dirt on them.» What does dirt mean here? | Loose soil where plants grow | A road with no hard surface | Gossip about someone | *Unclean stuff you can wash off
exercise: Gardeners say dirt is where plants grow and worms live. Which meaning is this? | Grease on a pan | Dust on a shelf | *Loose earth or soil | Dirt about someone
exercise: «Monkeys groom each other, picking out dirt, dead skin and bugs.» Which word means unclean matter picked out of fur? | monkeys | bugs | *dirt | groom
test: «Ben's sister told him some dirt about her best friend.» What does dirt mean here? | Loose soil in the garden | Mud on her shoes | *Gossip, or bad secret information about someone | Grease from the kitchen
test: «The shop sold the old bike dirt cheap.» What does dirt cheap mean? | Made of soil | Covered in mud | *Very cheap | Full of germs
exam: «A graze can go bad if dirt is left in it.» Why should you clean a graze? | Because dirt makes skin shiny | Because grazes always bleed | Because soil helps plants grow | *Because dirt left in it can cause an infection
